# ComfyUI models/outputs must never enter git (server lives at C:\ComfyUI anyway)
**/ComfyUI_windows_portable/
**/models/checkpoints/*.safetensors
# Third-party copyrighted source material — local reference only, never committed.
# The Doust booklet and every figure extracted from it: 17 figures are Doust's own
# and 31 belong to other named authors/publishers. NONE are cleared for
# redistribution yet, so neither the PDF nor the extracted PNGs may enter git or a
# deploy. Re-create locally with docs/arganta-energy/knowledge-base/extract_doust_figures.py
docs/arganta-energy/knowledge-base/doust-basin-figures/_source/
apps/energy/public/doust-figures/
# Basin figures harvested from publications: those extracted from USGS reports are
# US Government works (public domain) and DO ship — apps/energy/public/basin-figures/.
# Figures REPRODUCED inside a USGS report from a copyrighted source are not public
# domain, and anything pulled from paywalled literature certainly is not. The
# harvester routes those to the -restricted directory purely so this one rule can
# keep them out of a public repo. Never move a file across that boundary by hand.
apps/energy/public/basin-figures-restricted/
# Generated Markdown vault (9k+ notes) — rebuild from the workbook with
# docs/arganta-energy/knowledge-base/export_kb_markdown.py
docs/arganta-energy/knowledge-base/vault/

# USGS source archives and publication PDFs downloaded by the petroleum-system
# harvester. ~1.8 GB, and reg1/reg2/reg6.zip each exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard
# limit, so a push carrying them is rejected outright rather than merely slow.
# They are re-downloadable inputs, not source. Keep the scripts, drop the spoil.
.codex/tmp-petsys/sources/
.codex/tmp-petsys/monographs/
.codex/tmp-petsys/current-pubs/
# Workbook inspection dumps: build output, 55-90 MB each.
*.xlsx.inspect.ndjson
